# catalog/lane-run-inputs.d/dequeue-watch.rw — the files one
# `bin/dequeue-watch.sh <p>` run writes (BH-7424). A write-back may carry
# these only. The ro snapshot is these plus dequeue-watch.ro.
#
# NOT CARRIED (machine-local caches and logs, safe to lose):
#   $MC_H/tmp/merge-queue-*.provider (one-tick cache), state/gh-budget/*,
#   state/verdicts/route-missing-*, state/lead-authority/*,
#   logs/needs-human.log, logs/merge-conductor.log, logs/verdicts.log.
#   Alerts go through the jobs API when LANE_RUN_ID is set (bin/lane-alert.sh).
# Secrets and locks are never carried: env/*, locks/*.
# logs/dequeue-watch.log rides back as the lane log (.lri/log-append).
#
# MC_ATTEMPTS (bin/lib/mc/log.sh:53): mc_attempt_put "dqwculprit ..."
# (bin/lib/dequeue-watch/act.sh:258) and mc_requeued_record/mc_requeued_mark
# (bin/lib/mc/classify.sh:2443-2446). The same slice and ERE as
# merge-conductor.rw, so both lanes write back this repo's lines under the
# same attempts.txt.lock.
state/merge-conductor/attempts.txt
@rows state/merge-conductor/attempts.txt ^[^ ]+ $slug(#[0-9]+)?( |$)
# mc_mergify_ask_file (bin/lib/mc/queue.sh:1154): the `@mergifyio requeue`
# ask ledger, one file per PR, named by the folded repo.
state/merge-conductor/mergify-asked/$repokey_*
